# rbf-channel.env — the RBF channel's identity, in one record.
#
# Every fork-owned script and the icon generator read this file instead of
# restating its values, so changing the channel is mostly editing this file --
# but "only" would be a lie, and knowing where it stops is the useful part:
#
#   - install-rbf.sh hardcodes its DerivedData path (`cmux-rbf-cm-17-install`).
#     Deliberate: that is a build-artifact location, not channel identity, and
#     CMUX_RBF_DERIVED_DATA overrides it.
#   - The runtime icon assets are FILES (Assets.xcassets/AppIconLight-RBF...).
#     rbf/scripts/generate-rbf-runtime-icons.swift derives their names from
#     RBF_ICON_SET, but renaming the channel means re-running it and committing
#     the new imagesets; the record alone cannot move a PNG.
#   - Sources/AppIconDockTilePlugin.swift re-derives the same suffix by hand,
#     for reasons its own header states. It reads CFBundleIconName at runtime,
#     so it follows this record -- but it is a second copy of the derivation.
#
# Format is flat KEY="value" on purpose: shell `source`s it directly, and
# Python reads it with a partition("=") loop plus a strip of surrounding
# quotes. Neither side takes a dependency on the other, and neither owns it.
#
# THE QUOTES ARE LOAD-BEARING, not style. RBF_APP_NAME and RBF_INSTALL_PATH
# both contain a space; unquoted, `source` reads `RBF_APP_NAME=cmux` and then
# tries to run `RBF` as a command. Caught by the resolver test on first run.
#
# Keep it free of shell syntax beyond KEY=value — no command substitution, no
# conditionals, no references to other variables. The Python reader is
# deliberately dumb, and a value it cannot parse is a value that silently
# disagrees between the two readers.

# What the user sees: Dock, Cmd-Tab, Spotlight, the app menu.
RBF_APP_NAME="cmux RBF"

# The partition key for UserDefaults, Application Support and the socket.
# Irreversible: changing it orphans every workspace created under the old id.
RBF_BUNDLE_ID="com.cmuxterm.app.rbf"

# The nested dock tile plugin. MUST differ from RBF_BUNDLE_ID — a build-wide
# PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER= would collapse both onto one id, which is why the
# installer sets these per bundle with PlistBuddy after the build instead.
RBF_PLUGIN_BUNDLE_ID="com.cmuxterm.app.rbf.docktileplugin"

# Where the installed app lives. The resolver refuses anything else.
RBF_INSTALL_PATH="/Applications/cmux RBF.app"

# Asset catalog entry, generated by rbf/scripts/generate_rbf_icon.py.
RBF_ICON_SET="AppIcon-RBF"

# Banner colour and text for the generated icon. Third in the established
# series: AppIcon-Debug is orange DEV, AppIcon-Nightly is purple NIGHTLY.
# Three characters so it inherits the Debug icon's proven text metrics.
RBF_ICON_BANNER_TEXT="RBF"
RBF_ICON_BANNER_RGB="34,139,72"

# Info.plist key carrying the fork's own version. The installer WRITES it into
# every installed bundle; nothing READS it yet -- the About panel still shows
# upstream's inherited CFBundleShortVersionString / CFBundleVersion, which is why
# `env | grep CMUX_BUNDLE_ID` is currently the only honest answer to "which cmux
# am I in?". The reader lands in #cm-17.3. The key exists now so that slice finds
# the value already present in bundles installed before it.
RBF_VERSION_PLIST_KEY="RBFVersion"

# What the installer refuses to touch, under any code path.
UPSTREAM_BUNDLE_ID="com.cmuxterm.app"
UPSTREAM_INSTALL_PATH="/Applications/cmux.app"
